Our company, Faber IA, has experience working with public sector and health institutions, including a regional hospital group where we implemented an AI assistant for medical documentation. We understand the importance of data sovereignty and security, and our partnership with OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider (SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified), guarantees that CHRB's data is hosted within the European Union, ensuring compliance with GDPR and other regulatory requirements.

Our proposed solution, Atelier, is a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organization's own documents. It provides an intelligent assistance tool accessible from hospital staff's work environment, supporting clinical-administrative activities such as information consultation, drafting of medical and administrative documents, and handling dossiers. Atelier also facilitates continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, understanding the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and efficient resumption of handling by another professional.

In terms of technical requirements, our platform meets the needs for response times below 2 seconds for common queries, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and a p95 latency of less than 2 seconds. We also ensure high availability, with an availability target of 99.9%, and provide built-in monitoring, logging, and observability to guarantee this level of service. Our API-first design allows for seamless integration with CHRB's existing systems, including the hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), using standard connectors or custom adapters as needed.

We take data protection and security seriously, complying with GDPR, medical confidentiality, and HDS framework requirements. Our infrastructure is certified with HDS (Hébergeur de Données de Santé), ensuring the highest level of security for health data hosting. We also provide explainability and traceability features, including grounded-in-sources traceability, audit log, and support for a posteriori review, aligning with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare.

To ensure successful deployment, we propose a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement. This approach enables us to work closely with CHRB stakeholders throughout the project lifecycle, providing change management support and staff training to guarantee a smooth transition.

Our pricing model targets a gross margin between 25% and 35%, and we aim to optimize costs while ensuring the expected quality of service. We consider one-off project costs accounting for 30% of the budget and recurring run costs accounting for 70%, allowing us to propose strategies such as efficient tier selection, optimized resource allocation, phased implementation, and change management support to minimize expenses.

In terms of environmental sustainability, we are committed to reducing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure. Our partnership with OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, supports CHRB's goals in this area. We also practice digital sobriety, minimizing the environmental footprint of our operations through techniques such as model right-sizing, caching, and batching.

Our solution is designed to fit into existing practices without introducing disruptions, and we are committed to delivering high-quality service while respecting CHRB's budgetary capacity. We believe that our proposed AI assistance solution can effectively support CHRB's digital transformation goals, improving the efficiency of its staff and the quality and safety of care delivered to patients.

In conclusion, we are confident that our consortium, led by Faber IA, can deliver a tailored AI assistance solution that meets CHRB's specific needs and constraints. We look forward to collaborating with CHRB stakeholders to ensure successful deployment and provide high-quality service while respecting budgetary and environmental considerations.
